@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@
 <ul>
 <li>The top bar button now has the same spacing as the game's data layers button and other mods' buttons, so a row of buttons looks even.</li>
 <li>Fleet window redesigned in the game's own style: line, money and model table in the game's cards with their headings above them, shorter table headings (hover them for the full meaning), Upgrade buttons in the model table only when the line runs more than one model, and one row of buttons below. The explanation of the Upgrade buttons is now in their tooltips.</li>
+<li>Radar window tidied up in the same style: the alert list sits in one of the game's cards with alternating row shading, long names wrap instead of running into the next column, the vehicle type and line or depot show under the name, details get more room, "↑ Upg" sits at the end of its row, an empty tab shows its message at the top with the snooze options at the bottom, and the Settings tab has both columns at the top with each section in a card, values and ranges in straight columns and shorter labels (hover for the full explanation). Fewer stylesheet rules (31 → 21).</li>
 </ul>
